Found it. The root cause of the hang: in `populate_monsters` (src/core/game.rs:147), `random_floor_tile` is called with `&mut self.rng.clone()` — each call freshly clones the RNG, so unless the shared stream advances, it always proposes the same tile. If the proposed tile happens to be the player's position, nothing gets placed, the stream never advances, and the `while placed < n` loop spins forever. My change to `spawn_monster` shifted the stream by one draw (the species `pick`), and with seed 42 it now lands on a player position collision. The existing `max = n + 4` was intended as the cap on the number of attempts, but it's incorrectly applied to `placed` (which is always `< max`), so it doesn't bound the loop.

