## Goal
- Implement issue 21 (endless mode after amulet pickup) in the Rust roguelike at /home/anonymous/projects/rougelike, per AGENTS.md; run `cargo test` before committing; commit with a message referencing the issue.

## Constraints & Preferences
- User: follow AGENTS.md; run `cargo test` before committing; commit work with message referencing this issue; if fix needs discussion or is ambiguous, say so and stop WITHOUT committing.
- Issue file: /home/anonymous/projects/rougelike/.scratch/deepdelve/issues/21-endless-mode-unimplemented.md — acceptance criteria: amulet pickup offers endless choice (or trigger decided during implementation review of PLAN); declining ends run as today; choosing endless allows descending past old max depth; monsters beyond cap use existing scaling branch; run ends normally if declined.
- Out of scope per issue: new content tiers beyond existing scaling branch; endless-specific UI beyond the prompt.
- Repo convention (from prior issues 18/20, e.g. commits 9107717, 59d407b): implementation commit + separate "Mark issue N (...) as done" commit that sets `Status: done` and appends `Resolved (<hash>): ...` comment under `## Comments` in the issue file (tracker conventions in docs/agents/issue-tracker.md).

## Progress
### Done
- Explored codebase: located all endless plumbing (see Critical Context).
- Edited src/core/game.rs `try_stairs_down` (line ~658): now `let Some(next) = self.current_level.checked_add(1) else { return false; };` and cap is `if !self.endless && next > MAX_LEVELS { return false; }` — endless lifts the cap; non-endless behavior unchanged.
- Added `App::continue_endless()` in src/ui/app.rs (after `load_game`): sets `game.endless = true`, logs "Endless descent. The dungeon stretches on below.", calls `crate::save::autosave(game)`, sets `screen = Screen::Play`.
- Edited src/main.rs: victory render call now `menu::render_victory(f, s, game.turn, !game.endless)`; added key arm in `Screen::Death | Screen::Victory` branch: `KeyCode::Char('c') | KeyCode::Char('C')` guarded by `app.screen == Screen::Victory && app.game.as_ref().is_some_and(|g| g.won && !g.endless)` → `app.continue_endless()`; `KeyCode::Enter` still returns to title (decline path unchanged).

### In Progress
- src/ui/menu.rs `render_victory` still has the OLD 3-param signature `render_victory(frame, score: u64, turns: u64)` but main.rs now calls it with 4 args → WILL NOT COMPILE until menu.rs is updated.

### Blocked
- (none)

## Key Decisions
- Trigger design point (the issue's single open question): chose **victory-screen endless-continue** rather than prompt-on-pickup, because PLAN.md explicitly specifies it (§5 line 172: "Victory: take the Amulet... → victory screen with score → endless mode: D26+ generated on demand"; §6 line 266: "Victory screen: score breakdown, hiscore entry, then endless-continue or new run") and the issue explicitly defers the trigger to implementation review. Not ambiguous enough to stop — issue delegates the decision; all acceptance criteria still met (declining = Enter → title, identical to today's behavior).
- Victory check in game.rs (`check_victory`, ~line 1072) stays as-is: fires on amulet pickup at depth ≥25, sets `won=true`, records hiscore, deletes save. `endless` flag is set later on the victory screen.
- `save::autosave` skips when `!alive || won`, so `continue_endless` must explicitly call `autosave` to restore the autosave (it does).

## Next Steps
1. Update `render_victory` in src/ui/menu.rs: add 4th param (e.g. `endless_offered: bool`) and render a prompt line like "  [C]ontinue endless descent   [Enter] new run" (keep existing "Press Enter to return to the title." as the decline path when not offered).
